  "summary": "Four candidates explicitly apply self-attention encoder models to estimating battery remaining life. I rank [V0078] first because Fischer et al. (2023) report the strongest classification result, F1=0.94 on ToxiBench; [V0077] is next with El-Sayed et al. (2022) reporting AUROC=0.87 on CellLife. [V0080] applies the same transformer approach to ProtMap but reports test MAE=0.73, which is lower-is-better and not directly comparable with the classification scores; [V0079] reports accuracy=0.66 on GridWatch. Because five IDs are required, [V0084] is appended only as a same-task battery-remaining-life study on ProtMap with AUROC=0.84; its stated method is decentralised training without pooled records, so it is not direct evidence of a transformer application.",
